values
  (213, 'Changes to slice 3.4 after an independent review, before it merged. A brief is taken to send by one run only, atomically, and only while the person has not said "stop briefs"; a send that went quiet is tried again after ten minutes, three tries in all. A brief is sent only when something in it is new since the last one; what still waits on or for the person rides along but never sends a brief on its own. It is kept to one Slack message, with a link to the full brief in the web app. Text written by people or the model loses the characters that would make links, emphasis or code. A time zone that could not be read is asked again on a later run, and nobody gets a brief on a guessed clock. The fallback owner''s brief lists conflicts with nobody to decide them. A run stops starting sends after 20 seconds, and Slack calls time out after ten. Owner changes made by someone else, including a new area, are listed; a person''s own decisions are not. Briefs carry what the web app already shows everyone, including what listening found in private channels (199), now pushed to the people it concerns. Left for later: telling a person in the web app that they do not qualify for briefs', 'The review found that two overlapping reconcile runs, or a failure after Slack had the message, sent a brief twice; that one stale wait sent a brief every weekday; that a wait''s text could become a disguised link in a direct message from the bot; and that a failed time zone lookup sent briefs at night for a week. Each now has a test', 'active', 'the owner', '2026-11-26T00:00:00Z', 'import', '213')
on conflict (origin, origin_ref) where origin_ref is not null do nothing;
